# Trivy exceptions — each entry must state WHY it cannot be acted on, and will
# stop being needed the moment that changes. This is not a place to silence
# findings that are merely inconvenient.
#
# Both entries below are vendored INSIDE pip itself (pip/_vendor/vendor.txt).
# They are not installed as independent packages and cannot be upgraded
# separately — `pip install --upgrade msgpack setuptools` has no effect on
# them. The image already ships setuptools 84.0.0 and msgpack 1.2.1 as real
# packages; these are pip's private bundled copies.
#
# The only fix is a pip release that vendors newer versions. The image already
# pins pip>=26.1.2 and resolves to 26.2.1, the newest available. Re-check when
# pip next revendors and delete these lines.
#
# Verified 2026-08-18: docker run kscb:fixed cat \
#   /opt/venv/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt
#     msgpack==1.1.2
#     setuptools==70.3.0

# msgpack 1.1.2 vendored in pip 26.2.1 (real msgpack package is 1.2.1)
